  "message": "The compact‑and‑restart process works on the memory store that was added by the mechanic – a small LanceDB‑based table that holds the shared‑memory data. When you trigger a compact, the system clears the entries in that LanceDB store and then restarts the Toyota service. The language models themselves (Letta, Claude, etc.) don’t hold the persistent memory; they just read from or write to the LanceDB store, so the actual compaction happens there on the server side.",
